<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_SentinelGraveWard.xml            UtinniPatches - SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2 build pass

  scarlands_kit_spec.md §4 (Forgotten Sentinels). "Sentinel spawning rides
  existing vanilla plumbing: repair alcoves / grave-wards as buildings
  carrying vanilla CompSpawnerPawn with lordJob = RM_LordJob_DefendPerimeter
  — VERIFIED that comp is fully def-driven" (spec's own words). This is
  that building, wired to RUT_LordJob_SentinelDefend (the SpawnedPawnParams-
  ctor subclass that hands in the real RUT_SentinelDefend duty — see that
  class's own header for why the plain RM_ base class alone can't).

  Density/lore per the spec's own §4: "SPARSE... most strongpoints are
  bones, the manned one is the exception... reads as SELF-REPAIR — surface
  Sentinels are the Cathedral's lost, self-mending, slowly devolving units,
  not a garrison being restocked." pawnSpawnIntervalDays (4~6) and the small
  points cap below are this build pass's own INVENTED-BUILD numbers for
  "ward scale, never a production line" — the spec names no figure
  ("spawner points cap per site still INVENTED", SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2.md's
  own spike-pass note).

  spawnablePawnKinds: PLACEHOLDER. vanilla Mech_Pikeman — a real, defensive,
  ranged mechanoid — stands in for the actual Forgotten Sentinel PawnKindDef,
  which does not exist anywhere in src/ yet (checked) and is roster/faction-
  pass content this kit does not own (the kit spec's own naming section:
  RUT_-tier CONTENT, "remaining content (§2-5) is RUT_-tier, owed to later
  passes" — a Sentinel's own kind/art/faction is exactly that kind of
  content, not this kit's mechanism work). Swap this one line for the real
  kind the moment the roster pass ships it; nothing else here changes.

  lordJoinRadius 80 (== defendRadius): CompSpawnerPawn.Lord/FindLordToJoin
  (decompile-confirmed) searches for an existing lord of the SAME lordJob
  TYPE within lordJoinRadius (vanilla default ~2.1B, i.e. "anywhere on the
  map") before spawning a new one — left at vanilla's huge default, every
  grave-ward on a map would pool its Sentinels into ONE lord defending
  whichever ward spawned first. Tightened to the ward's own defend radius so
  each grave-ward's Sentinels join only pawns from THAT ward (or one very
  nearby), each defending its own point — this build pass's own
  INVENTED-BUILD choice, undocumented in the spec.

  ✅ BUILT (SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2, 2026-09-26): faction assignment and map
  placement. CompSpawnerPawn.TrySpawnPawn spawns with parent.Faction
  (decompile-confirmed) — Faction is a runtime Thing property, never a
  ThingDef field, so it could not be set here in this def; a placement
  GenStep was the only route. `RUT_GenStep_ScatterSentinelGraveWards`
  (src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/, wired via
  Defs/MapGeneration/RUT_ScarlandsGraveWardScatter.xml into
  RUT_Scarlands.xml's own extraGenSteps) is the plain GenStep this needed —
  same shape as RUT_SacredWall_Conduit.xml's own precedent
  (RustCathedralWalls, same "Forgotten"/Cathedral lore family):
  `.SetFaction(Faction.OfMechanoids)` at placement time, the SAME faction
  (vanilla `Mechanoid`, hidden/permanentEnemy, reskinned "the Forgotten
  Arsenal" per ForgottenArsenal.xml), not a new one. Before this GenStep
  shipped, a debug-spawned RUT_SentinelGraveWard produced faction-less
  ("wild") Sentinels; now every grave-ward placed by that GenStep is
  Mechanoid-factioned from the moment it's spawned, so its own Sentinels
  inherit real hostility from CompSpawnerPawn's very first spawn. No
  live/quicktest verification yet — no bridge access this pass; see
  SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2.md.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: Things/Building/Linked/AncientFortifiedWall_Atlas — the
  REAL vanilla-Odyssey texture RimSage confirms AncientFortifiedWall itself
  ships with, tinted toward the grave-ward's own weathered-verdigris
  palette. 🔴 KNOWN validate_patch.py FALSE POSITIVE, not a real miss:
  ALL vanilla textures live inside Unity asset bundles, never as loose
  files (confirmed this pass: zero *.png anywhere under the live Data/
  root), so the checker can never resolve ANY vanilla texPath by design —
  it only escalates WARN to ERROR here because UtinniPatches ships its own
  Textures/Things/ folder (RUT_SacredWall_Conduit.xml, checked standalone
  outside that mod context, gets the softer WARN for the exact same class
  of miss on its own vanilla-styled path, with the tool's own text saying
  so: "cannot be called a typo... a correct vanilla path looks identical to
  a wrong one from here"). Same pre-existing, repo-wide pattern as
  RUT_VaultHeart.xml's own Things/Building/Ship/ShipComputerCore reuse
  (StructureInjectionsRUT, also owns its own Things/ namespace). Recorded
  as a known false positive in SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2.md rather than swapped
  for a worse-fitting texture just to silence the scanner. Real bespoke
  grave-ward art is owed (art pipe), same posture as every other
  placeholder in this kit.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_SentinelGraveWard</defName>
    <thingClass>Building</thingClass>
    <label>Sentinel grave-ward</label>
    <description>A squat, patterned monument half-sunk into the crust, still faintly warm. It does not explain itself. It does not need to — whatever it protects, it protects it still.</description>
    <category>Building</category>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>0.6</fillPercent>
    <coversFloor>false</coversFloor>
    <blockLight>false</blockLight>
    <blockWind>false</blockWind>
    <neverMultiSelect>true</neverMultiSelect>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <mineable>false</mineable>
    <leaveResourcesWhenKilled>false</leaveResourcesWhenKilled>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <staticSunShadowHeight>0.5</staticSunShadowHeight>
    <size>(2,2)</size>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Linked/AncientFortifiedWall_Atlas</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
      <color>(120,110,100)</color>
      <colorTwo>(90,40,45)</colorTwo>
      <drawSize>(2,2)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>800</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Beauty>-2</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <building>
      <deconstructible>false</deconstructible>
    </building>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_SpawnerPawn">
        <spawnablePawnKinds>
          <!-- PLACEHOLDER, see header. -->
          <li>Mech_Pikeman</li>
        </spawnablePawnKinds>
        <lordJob>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RUT_LordJob_SentinelDefend</lordJob>
        <defendRadius>80</defendRadius>
        <lordJoinRadius>80</lordJoinRadius>
        <initialPawnsCount>2</initialPawnsCount>
        <maxSpawnedPawnsPoints>300</maxSpawnedPawnsPoints>
        <pawnSpawnIntervalDays>4~6</pawnSpawnIntervalDays>
        <pawnSpawnRadius>3</pawnSpawnRadius>
        <chooseSingleTypeToSpawn>true</chooseSingleTypeToSpawn>
        <showNextSpawnInInspect>false</showNextSpawnInInspect>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
